<slide id="kano_rollout">
  <background color="paper"/>
  <shape id="top-bar" type="rect" x="0" y="0" width="1280" height="3" fill="brand-green"/>
  <text id="title" x="58" y="40" width="980" height="46" font="heading" size="30" color="ink" wrap="false">Kano can phase modernization without disrupting service</text>
  <text id="subtitle" x="58" y="86" width="1096" height="30" font="body" size="16" color="muted">The platform supports a phased implementation path that begins with urgent land-administration discipline and then expands into broader GIS, field, certification, and post-title control.</text>

  <shape id="phase1" type="rect" x="58" y="176" width="262" height="244" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="phase1t" x="82" y="202" width="214" height="178" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="brand-green">Phase 1</strong></p><p space-before="10"><strong>Registry and workflow backbone</strong></p><p space-before="10">Deploy parcel records, case visibility, certification workflow control, and audit-grade oversight for core land-administration operations.</p></text>

  <shape id="phase2" type="rect" x="342" y="176" width="262" height="244" fill="#EFF6FF" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="phase2t" x="366" y="202" width="214" height="178" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="accent-blue">Phase 2</strong></p><p space-before="10"><strong>Field and GIS continuity</strong></p><p space-before="10">Expand into demarcation, web parcel maps, field evidence continuity, and stronger desk-to-site alignment.</p></text>

  <shape id="phase3" type="rect" x="626" y="176" width="262" height="244" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="phase3t" x="650" y="202" width="214" height="178" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="brand-green">Phase 3</strong></p><p space-before="10"><strong>AI-assisted throughput and quality control</strong></p><p space-before="10">Add document parsing, verification support, and cleaner intake to improve speed without losing reviewer control.</p></text>

  <shape id="phase4" type="rect" x="910" y="176" width="312" height="244" fill="#EFF6FF" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="phase4t" x="934" y="202" width="264" height="178" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.3"><p><strong color="accent-blue">Phase 4</strong></p><p space-before="10"><strong>Revenue modernization and statewide scale</strong></p><p space-before="10">Layer in post-title transaction visibility, executive dashboards, and broader rollout across land-administration and related approval workflows.</p></text>

  <shape id="note-band" type="rect" x="58" y="548" width="1164" height="46" fill="#FEFCE8" stroke="#FDE68A" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="note" x="84" y="562" width="1112" height="18" font="body" size="15" color="ink" align="center" wrap="false">This phased path lets Kano start with its most urgent workflow and registry pain points while preserving a clear route to GIS-backed revenue modernization.</text>

  <text id="outcome" x="58" y="620" width="1040" height="28" font="body" size="19" color="ink">The platform can begin where administrative pressure is highest and expand without replacing the underlying operational backbone.</text>
  <text id="footer" x="58" y="686" width="620" height="18" font="caption" size="12" color="muted" wrap="false">IDLR-PTS Platform | Kano State</text>
  <text id="page" x="1210" y="684" width="22" height="18" font="caption" size="12" color="muted" align="right" wrap="false">8</text>
